# Launch-readiness audit, SEC-014.
#
# GitHub Pages cannot set response headers, so the app's CSP lives in a
# <meta> tag - and `frame-ancestors` is SPEC-IGNORED in a meta CSP. The
# result is that the app has NO clickjacking protection in production
# today, which matters because ~19 destructive actions sit behind a
# confirm sheet that a framing attacker could bait a click onto.
#
# This file is the Netlify/Cloudflare Pages format. It is inert on GitHub
# Pages (harmless), and becomes the fix the moment the site is fronted by
# a host that reads it. See docs/deploy/HEADERS.md for nginx/Cloudflare
# Workers equivalents and for what to verify after switching.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), usb=(), payment=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
